invalid-aliases.js:7:16 lint/nursery/noVueRefObjectReactivityLoss ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This reads the value of a ref only once, so it won't update when the ref changes.
  
    5 │ const count = ref(0)
    6 │ const alias = count
  > 7 │ const value1 = alias.value
      │                ^^^^^^^^^^^
    8 │ 
    9 │ let later
  
  i This code runs only once, together with the code that creates the ref. The value read here is a copy, and Vue does not update it when the ref changes.
  
  i Read .value inside a function, such as a computed() getter, or pass the ref itself instead of its value.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

